## Renders a nonempty vector of plot specifications as looping 800 by 400 GIF frames.
##
## **Signature:** `plot_save_gif : (String, Tensor<1, PlotSpec>, Int) -> IO Result<Unit, IOError>`
##
## Pass an Int delay from 0 through 65535 in hundredths of a second. The unqualified two-argument call uses a delay of 10. The allocation limit permits up to 312 frames. The IO action returns Ok(()) or Err(IOError).
##
## **Examples:**
## ```text
## import Plot as Plots
## Plots.plot_save_gif("anim.gif", [Plots.combine([Plots.line([0.0, 1.0], [0.0, 1.0])])], 25)
## ```
##
## *Source: Aevia standard library guide.*
